# Engineering practices

Write product code under `src/` to current Microsoft guidance for .NET, ASP.NET Core, Blazor, Entity Framework Core, Aspire, and xUnit.

These accepted decisions stay as they are:

- **Styling.** Theme and layout live in typed C# and MudBlazor parameters. Do not add `*.razor.css`. Hand-written CSS is only the loading screen and the unhandled-error bar in `wwwroot/css/app.css`.
- **Aspire.** Do not add a service-defaults project. The API stays on `5009` and `7011`, the Blazor app on `5186` and `7211`, and Postgres on `5432`.
- **Sign-in.** The session stays in the `HttpOnly` cookie `courtflow-session`. Page code does not read a WorkOS token. Who is signed in still comes from `GET /api/me`.
- **Dates.** A calendar date a director sees uses `MM/dd/yyyy`. The API keeps `yyyy-MM-dd`.

Do not change director-facing behavior, an API contract, or behavior an accepted intent specifies. When Microsoft guidance would change one of those, keep the accepted behavior.

`src/Directory.Build.props` holds `AnalysisLevel` `latest`, `AnalysisMode` `Recommended`, `TreatWarningsAsErrors` `true`, and `EnforceCodeStyleInBuild` `true`. Leave info-level suggestions off. Generated migration files stay generated. A suppression needs a reason beside it. Do not add one to make the build pass.

Google OR-Tools, hosted Postgres, and `tools/logo/` are outside this rule. Package versions belong to the current-packages rule.

Checking a branch against this rule is the `verify-engineering-practices` skill.
